{"created": "2026-07-03T01:27:23.075589+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-03T01:27:23.501044+00:00", "id": 20189813, "conceptrecid": "20189812", "doi": "10.64898/2026.05.29.728810", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.05.29.728810", "metadata": {"title": "RAD manuscript, R workspaces for figure generation", "doi": "10.64898/2026.05.29.728810", "publication_date": "2026-05-19", "description": "<p>R workspace files (<code>.RData</code>) containing all intermediate and final analysis objects used to produce Figures 2&ndash;5 of the RAD manuscript (<span class=\"highwire-cite-metadata-doi highwire-cite-metadata\">https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.05.29.728810v1.full</span>).</p>\n<p>Each <code>figure_N_workspace.RData</code> corresponds to one figure and is consumed by the matching R Markdown notebook in the companion GitHub repository <a href=\"https://github.com/indianewok/rad-manuscript\">indianewok/rad-manuscript</a>.</p>\n<p>Loading a workspace restores all named objects referenced by the figure's Rmd, allowing the figures to be rendered without the underlying raw FASTQ data. Per-workspace contents are documented in <code>data/README.md</code> of the GitHub repo.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Vaidya, Chinmay M.", "affiliation": "Geisel School of Medicine at Dartmouth"}], "keywords": ["single-cell sequencing", "long-read sequencing", "Oxford Nanopore", "barcode demultiplexing", "immune receptor", "B-cell receptor", "spatial transcriptomics", "RAD", "reproducibility"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/indianewok/rad-manuscript", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/indianewok/rad", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid